s is that when you have  it in this orientation they actually  switch when you flip it so at this point  this is going to be the top if you  switch it the other way it flips in  software automatically which is really  really clever by apple now one of the  most important changes is that apple  finally gave the mini the usb type c  port and got rid of lightning this is  going to be extremely important because  usb type-c takes a lot more power and it  allows you to connect to more devices  whereas lightning is very very limited  and on top of that you can see that we  have speaker grills on the bottom but on  the new mini 6 you actually get a set on  the top now i know this next detail is  going to annoy some of you guys out  there but the ipad mini 6 no longer gets  a headphone jack which sucks but really  for us it's not that big of a deal now  before i show you guys the major changes  to touch id and everything else i do  want to mention that along with the new  redesign of the ipad mini 6 apple  actually did pack in extra magnets  throughout the internals just like on  the ipad pro and the ipad air so now the  new smartfolio actually connects on both  the back side and the front side using  just those internal magnets whereas on  the ipad mini 5 it actually connected to  the side and only covered the front so  you're getting a lot of protection and  this actually looks really nice and  clean because just how slim this folio  is like this is awesome now flipping  over to the front side let's go ahead  and just  boot up this ipad mini for the first  time but i do want to mention the design  differences  finally this old design with the white  bezels the home button is gone we now  have the new modern version with the  rounded corners on the display and those  even uniform bezels which obviously  looks much much better now along with  all those huge changes the other major  difference is touch id is now built into  the power button so i'm going to show  you guys the process right here  and as you can see i'm just  touching the power button just like that  and it is registering my  fingerprint now if you're wondering if  the new power button touch id is any  faster it is not because we actually  tested it with the ipad air and there  was no difference and even though this  is kind of cool to have that new touch  id i'd actually say that it's a little  bit more annoying because with the ipad  mini 5 you just go like this you tap the  button and it unlocks just like that but  with the mini you have to reach up and  hit it up there which can be a little  bit more annoying than just having it on  the face but either way it allows the  display to be obviously much more clean  like that now as far as the displays  because apple got rid of that home  button and the chins the actual ipad  mini 6 itself does get a little bit  shorter but it gets a little bit  skinnier on the sides because of those  slightly larger bezels compared to the  side on the ipad mini 6 but what that  gives you is basically the widest aspect  ratio in terms of watching videos which  is definitely a nice difference and in  terms of the hand i'd say that i  actually like the ipad mini 6 and how it  feels with those boxy edges compared to  the old chamfered edges which seem kind  of  slippery and of course the new mini 6  does have a larger 8.3 inch display  compared to 7.9 and because you're  getting rid of those extra distractions  like the home button and the chins this  is definitely a much more immersive  display even if it's not that much  bigger only five percent in terms of the  actual screen real estate and now with  all that display and design stuff out of  the way let's go ahead and jump into the  speaker comparison and see how much  better they are on the mini  we'll six started  [Music]  all right wow guys we've never really  complained about the ipad mini 5s  speakers they were always pretty good we  just complained that they were on one  side but now we have a huge improvement  on basically every level just having the  stereo speakers on both sides is  basically a 5x  times game changer in terms of speaker  quality however the old ipad mini 5  speakers they seem like they were tuned  for the high ends and you're missing out  on a lot of those mid band frequencies  like you're not really getting the  dynamic range between all the little  instruments and everything else but this  has like this richness to it where the  mids are clear you can hear them such a  huge difference with the new mini 6  compared to any old ipad mini  crazy with that out of the way let's  finally go and test the performance  starting out with geek match 5. you guys  can see that we're actually getting 4  gigs of ram on the mini 6 compared to  only three let's start off with the cpu  benchmark and while this test is running  i do want to mention that the mini 6 has  the brand new a15 bionic chip from the  iphone 13 it's not quite as fast because  it is down clocked to help save battery  life and the ipad mini 5 gets the old  a12 chip that is a pretty old chip it's  even older than the new ipad 9 with the  a13 so let's see how big of a difference  there is all right we have our scores  and this is an awesome difference going  from generation to generation for the  ipad mini we're going from 1114  single core to 1590  that is a 43  difference which is awesome now  interestingly the a15 single core is not  as high as on the iphone 13s so it's  definitely down clocked but if we go  over to the multi-core we're going from  2786 to 45.41  that is a 63  improvement which is awesome and this is  actually scoring close to the iphone 13  pro max so it seems like our theory on  whether the efficiency cores are much  faster is true they are much faster so  this is definitely a nice difference  let's go ahead and get into the compute  metal graphics test now while this is  running i do want to mention that apple  did not cheap out on the graphics on the  ipad mini 6 with the a15 because it does  get the new 5 core gpu so you're getting  the extra core on top of what you have  in the a12 and because of that we're not  just getting a 30 or 50 generational  improvement not even double we're  getting 2.63  times  faster graphics performance than the  ipad mini 5 which blows my mind so the  gaming performance on this is  insane and speaking of gaming let's see  how it fares in a real gaming benchmark  and 2-2 bench so let's go ahead and  start the antutu benchmark all right  guys just watching this playback the  ipad mini 6 literally perfectly smooth  and you're getting dropped frames  already on the ipad mini 5 even though  both displays are 60 hertz there is a  noticeable difference in terms of the  fps and smoothness we've got a score and  this is very interesting on two  different levels first of all the  performance difference is uh 42 higher  for the mini 6 which isn't as much as it  was before because this kind of factors  in everything and it's a real world test  but  this school right here 771 000 is very  impressive because the iphone 13 pro max  which is supposed to have faster chips  in terms of the cpu and gpu was only  slightly faster with 788 and the reason  for that is because the iphone suffers  from thermal throttling it overheats and  in these longer term benchmarks it has  to kind of slow down a bit but it looks  like the ipad mini doesn't have to  because it's larger and it dissipates  heat better this thing is impressive for  gaming photo editing video editing  basically anything that you can do on  this tablet it's gonna kill it and the  last thing i want to test in terms of  the performance is the ssd storage speed  so we have jazz disk test right here  let's go ahead and run it and with that  said we do actually get faster ssds in  the mini six you can see the write speed  is almost twice as fast 595 megabytes  per second compared to 266 the read  speeds are basically the same and in  terms of the iops you're getting 33  megabytes per second compared to 22 for  the read and 19 compared to 12 so that's  nice to see that even though they're 64  gigs we do get faster store speeds now  before i get into the conclusion and  answer the original question let's get  into those cameras because we do have  some differences obviously we have the  camera bump on the mini 6 and it is now  a 12 megapixel sensor with an f 1.8 lens  compared to f 2.4 so it's gonna let in  more light and it's gonna have more  resolution and if you're someone who  likes to scan documents the extra flash  on the mini 6 is definitely going to be  helpful and then flipping over to the  front side the mini 5 has a 7 megapixel  selfie camera and the new mini 6  actually has a 12 megapixel ultra wide  and what i mean by that is  boom you can go into ultrawide you can  do that linus meme face but there you go  you have that crazy ultra wide view  which looks really cool it's definitely  a unique perspective and this helps it  support the new center stage feature now  unfortunately because of the ultra wide  camera when you take a regular selfie  like this it's actually not as detailed  as the 7 megapixel sensor on the mini 5  and that's also why you can't shoot 4k  video with the selfie cam because it's  ultra wide so it crops in and gives you  1080p but it can go up to 60 fps which  the ipad mini 5 cannot do all right with  all of that said and compared let's  finally answer the original question  is it worth upgrading to the ipad mini 6  and the only thing i can say is  yes yes it is even at the higher price  of 500 which some people were  complaining about  this ipad basically fixes everything it  fixes the biggest issues that we had  with the ipad mini 5 and you're  basically getting the best of all worlds  you're getting killer speakers you're  getting the new design that's going to  be modern and future proof for years on  end you're getting excellent cameras  you're getting killer performance  performance that's only beaten by the m1  ipad pro which is already overkill for  everything you can't even use all that  power so with this thing for 500  that is actually a killer value for  everything that you're getting and if  you have even the ipad mini 5 or any of  the older ipad minis or even the other  ipads this thing's insane you've got to  upgrade to this so there you guys go as  you can tell i'm super excited and happy  about the ipad mini 6. apple did an  excellent job and even at 500  it's a killer value and definitely a  worthy upgrade so hopefully you guys  enjoyed this video and if you did go  ahead and subscribe because we have a  ton more videos that we're working on  and definitely watch one of those two  right over there thanks for watching and  we'll see you in the next video  [Music]

